  "id": "Compound::DB00536 - Gene::56479",
  "verbalization": "Guanidine appears to interact with potassium channels through a shared mechanism of involvement in delayed rectifier potassium channel activity, as evidenced by its binding to Kcna6, Kcnv2, and Kcna7, all of which participate in this activity. This suggests that Guanidine may modulate potassium channel function by influencing the activity of these channels, potentially through a common pathway. The involvement of Kcnq5 in this activity, as indicated by the \"is participated by\" relationship, implies that Guanidine could either directly affect Kcnq5 or indirectly influence its function through other channels. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust connection, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence points to a role for Guanidine in regulating potassium channel activity, with Kcnq5 being a downstream target in this process.",
